	(text "The bank voltage determines which I/O standards can be used on its signals.\nConfiguration, Ethernet, USB FIFO and matrix-control signals must follow their\nactual bank assignments. The DDR banks must retain the DDR1V35 supply and\nthe reference connections shown on the DDR3L sheet."
